{
  "title": "Extra-abdominal Desmoid Tumor",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8062/extra-abdominal-desmoid-tumor",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 3 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Extra-abdominal Desmoid Tumors are benign, locally aggressive, fibrogenic lesions that are associated with familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in patients between the ages of 25 and 35 with a firm, enlarging soft tissue mass",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy showing well-differentiated fibroblasts with uniform spindle cells with elongated nuclei and occasional mitoses. Immunohistochemistry will show a positive stain for estrogen receptor-beta.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be medical management with tamoxifen or wide surgical excision with radiotherapy depending on the size, grade and location of the lesion.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "900 cases a year in US",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "younger individuals (25-35 years of age)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "female>male (3:1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "higher incidence in familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP) and Gardner syndrome 4-30%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cortical desmoid lesions affect active adolescents",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common shoulder (20%) > chest wall/back (17%) > thigh (13%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": ">50% are extra-abdominal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may have multiple lesions in the same extremity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "subsequent mass usually appears more **proximally** in the same limb",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "appears in sites of previous surgery or scars",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cortical desmoid lesions result from chronic tendon traction injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common location involves posteromedial femur at medial head of gastrocnemius or adductor magnus insertion site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patient's with **familial adenomatous polyposis** (FAP) have increased risk for development of desmoid tumors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "15% of tumors have adenomatous polyposis coli (APC) gene mutation (gene controls beta catenin)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "elevated levels of **beta catenin** in all tumors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "trisomy in **chromosome 8 or 20**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Dupuytren contractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Ledderhose disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Gardner syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Symptoms",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Presentation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**usually an enlarging mass**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**nerve compression**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "numbness, tingling, motor weakness, stabbing pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "has a distinctive \"rock hard\" feel on palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "because tumor is fixed to surrounding tissues",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "poorly circumscribed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be painful and limit motion around joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "play minimal role in diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "some tumors encroach on/erode bone or trigger periosteal reaction that extends into tumor as \"frond like\" spicules of bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "best means to diagnose",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "exclude multicentric lesions (in the same extremity)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "low signal intensity on T1-weighted images",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "low to medium intensity on T2-weighted images",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Gadolinium enhances appearance",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "infiltrates muscle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "5-10cm in size",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may erode bone locally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Gross specimen",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "gritty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "white",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "poorly encapsulated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Classic characteristics are",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8062/images/extra%20abdominal%20desmoid%20tumor.jpg",
                  "caption": "Extra abdominal desmoid tumor"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "well-differentiated fibroblasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "uniform spindle cells with elongated nuclei and occasional mitoses",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "abundant collagen",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tumor infiltrates adjacent tissues",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Molecular Genetics/Immunohistochemisty",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**100% positive for estrogen receptor-beta**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "somatostatin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cathepsin D",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Ki-67",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "c-Kit",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "negative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "estrogen receptor-alpha",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "progesterone receptor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "HER2",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Watch and wait with serial MRI examinations to monitor for progression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "vast majority of cases, particularly asymptomatic or minimally symptomatic, may be managed initially with a period of",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "monitoring",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tumors may remain stable and even regress over time",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cortical desmoid tumors in young adolescents are self-limiting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "low dose-chemotherapy only / tamoxifen",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "inoperable lesions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tamoxifen favored for failed/poor candidates for standard chemotherapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "works because most lesions occur in women and are more aggressive in women, especially premenopausal",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "tamoxifen works via an estrogen receptor blockage",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wide surgical resection with radiotherapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symptomatic lesion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "recurrent lesion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "local recurrence is common (reduced recurrence with radiotherapy)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "external beam radiation dose 50-60Gy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "margin negative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "28% recurrence with surgery alone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "6% recurence with surgery + radiation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "margin positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "39% recurence with surgery alone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "25% recurernce with surgery + radiation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "High risk of recurrence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Highly unpredictable lesions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Occasional spontaneous regression",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "No risk of metastasis or malignant transformation, unless related to radiation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
